<title>NEW ZEALAND: POLL - Updated Reuters survey of NZ current account.</title>
<headline>POLL - Updated Reuters survey of NZ current account.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a revised table of economists' forecasts for New Zealand balance of payments data for the March quarter, due on Friday, July 11. Averages, medians and ranges have changed from those previously published as Garlick and Co Ltd has revised its forecasts and Bancorp's have been included.</p>
<p>Times are GMT.</p>
<p>DAY TIME INDICATOR	     PERIOD     AVG F/CAST   PREVIOUS</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Fri 2245 Balance of payments</p>
<p>    a   NZ$ million		 Mar qtr   -212.2	   -1,292</p>
<p>    b   NZ$ million		 Yr-Mar    -4,111	   -3,913</p>
<p>    c   Pct of GDP		  at Mar 31  4.39 pct	 4.2 pct</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Further information:</p>
<p>    FORECAST  RESPONDENTS  MEDIAN	 RANGE</p>
<p>    a	   11	    -240 million     -450 million to +100 million</p>
<p>    b	   11	    -4,140 million   -4,347 million to -3,800 million</p>
<p>    c	   11	     4.2 pct	4.1 pct to 4.7 pct</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Respondents to the survey -  ANZ Bank (NZ) Ltd, ASB Bank, Bancorp, Bankers Trust New Zealand, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, Doyle Paterson Brown, First NZ Capital, Garlick and Co Ltd, National Bank of New Zealand, SBC Warburg, WestpacTrust.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
